# Sentiment Analysis System

A beginner-friendly sentiment analysis application built with Python, NLTK, scikit-learn, and Streamlit. The project demonstrates a reusable NLP preprocessing pipeline, robust dataset validation, model training and evaluation, and a polished web frontend for single-text and batch sentiment analysis.

## Features

- Text sentiment classification for Positive, Negative, and Neutral labels
- Probability and confidence output for each class
- Reusable preprocessing utilities for URLs, HTML, punctuation, negation, and lemmatization
- Dataset validation and class distribution reporting
- TF-IDF + bigram + logistic regression training pipeline
- Held-out evaluation with accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score
- Streamlit dashboard, analyzer, batch analysis, evaluation, and dataset explorer pages
- Safe handling for empty, malformed, or unexpected input

## Technology stack

- Python 3.10+
- Streamlit
- Pandas
- NumPy
- scikit-learn
- NLTK
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Pytest

